# promise: #345
# A double-click on the favicon of a pinned tab away from its pinned page takes it back there
# once (#345), as a single click there does (Arc's icon region, #139). Before the fix its second
# press counted as a new click: back to back (as here) it loaded the pinned page a second time,
# and a hand's ~150 ms later, on a tab already home, it opened the rename field
# (PinnedIconClickTests covers that timing). The clicks go through the event queue to the row,
# as the pointer's would; the page reads where it is.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=home
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://action/pinTab
wait 1
cra://debug?cdp=Page.navigate&params={"url":"${PAGE}?n=away"}
wait 1.5
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"'at=' + location.search"}
expect-log "value":"at=\?n=away"
# The only tab row is the pinned tab's; its favicon is 18 pt in from the row's leading edge.
cra://debug?snapshot=TabRowView&out=/dev/null
expect-log snapshot: TabRowView at 8,234 size 312x40

# A double-click on the favicon goes back once and leaves the name alone.
cra://debug?clickAt=26,254&clicks=2
expect-log pinned icon: back to pinned URL
expect-log pinned icon: a double-click's second press stays home
wait 1.5
reject-log sidebar double-click: rename
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"'double=' + location.search"}
expect-log "value":"double=\?n=home"

# On its pinned page the favicon is the row's again: a double-click renames the tab.
cra://debug?clickAt=26,254&clicks=2
expect-log sidebar double-click: rename
cra://debug?checkStore=1
